<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Manjaro on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/manjaro/</link><description>Recent content in Manjaro on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 28 Feb 2014 12:08:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/manjaro/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Installing Ruby Rails on Manjaro Linux</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/installing-ruby-rails-on-manjaro-linux/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Feb 2014 12:08:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/installing-ruby-rails-on-manjaro-linux/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Thought I'd give Rails another go on my newly created Manjaro Linux VM.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhAY-9P0iuvGBpUXG9-rrKgREuzE-j2CqdrKToThQTsoovZWMp4GYUe205L03o9LH5VwJsI4zV6Hk9wY_5_ps_m3THhr2vHkWs5-fYcOgWHcBqEuv_IuvWkhVrWts656Yd3omDC6UsPylY/s1600/Manjaro+Rails.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhAY-9P0iuvGBpUXG9-rrKgREuzE-j2CqdrKToThQTsoovZWMp4GYUe205L03o9LH5VwJsI4zV6Hk9wY_5_ps_m3THhr2vHkWs5-fYcOgWHcBqEuv_IuvWkhVrWts656Yd3omDC6UsPylY/s1600/Manjaro+Rails.png" height="184" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;After filling in a couple of required packages the above screenshot shows it firing through the Rails install.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;To get to this stage I did the following;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;ul style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;,Courier,monospace;"&gt;sudo pacman -S base-devel ruby sqlite3 nodejs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Added &lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;,Courier,monospace;"&gt;/home/alastair/.gem/ruby/2.1.0/bin&lt;/span&gt; to my path in .bashrc &lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;,Courier,monospace;"&gt;gem install rails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;,Courier,monospace;"&gt;gem install execjs &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;After a few minutes got the following successful install&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg1tm8RGzy6qE1OkPDK9KenjY3ltDKGDgRrgOTTPNqCrHw1-47CqdgaQBuyZr_uL24ON5NFxP4YkNjm4AsVr931CPMR2G2morv8ybd58tJkC2U83DbKc7UMt2RW7M8A8X4LOtckwpT_0Bo/s1600/Manjaro+Rails2.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg1tm8RGzy6qE1OkPDK9KenjY3ltDKGDgRrgOTTPNqCrHw1-47CqdgaQBuyZr_uL24ON5NFxP4YkNjm4AsVr931CPMR2G2morv8ybd58tJkC2U83DbKc7UMt2RW7M8A8X4LOtckwpT_0Bo/s1600/Manjaro+Rails2.png" height="184" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Now to dig out that Rails tutorial I was working through.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Update&lt;/b&gt;,&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Turns out can't start a rails server do it a missing JavaScript Runtime, bit more searching require.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Update2&lt;/b&gt;,&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Found the answer on the Arch Linux Wiki which worked updated the instructions above.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;ul style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, Courier, monospace;"&gt;sudo pacman -S nodejs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;Success&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjC_jMQgtCeY4Fv0_6ghJMGdqbTSPv2MZQdmVgfiZ8sVh5ZEb9mLW1gaKCb0RcRxB-TRHc3iWEyMOjFX2p8QvR7xWGllo5RKRUiMLaKtYLb7nGTS72nUu6jci2iPJXa-VHYXCLK91OaGQc/s1600/Manjaro+Rails3.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjC_jMQgtCeY4Fv0_6ghJMGdqbTSPv2MZQdmVgfiZ8sVh5ZEb9mLW1gaKCb0RcRxB-TRHc3iWEyMOjFX2p8QvR7xWGllo5RKRUiMLaKtYLb7nGTS72nUu6jci2iPJXa-VHYXCLK91OaGQc/s1600/Manjaro+Rails3.png" height="184" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Manjaro Linux Openbox</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/manjaro-linux-openbox/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Feb 2014 14:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/manjaro-linux-openbox/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="font-size: 0.8em; line-height: 1.6em; margin: 0 0 10px 0; padding: 0;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/12793203984/" title="Manjaro Linux Openbox"&gt;&lt;img alt="Manjaro Linux Openbox by Alastair Montgomery" src="https://farm4.staticflickr.com/3806/12793203984_9b37719f63.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="margin: 0;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/12793203984/"&gt;Manjaro Linux Openbox&lt;/a&gt;, a photo by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt; on Flickr.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;i&gt;Via Flickr:&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Based on Arch Linux so seems pretty nippy at the moment in the VM.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Upload from Dropbox February 26, 2014 at 01:46PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Manjaro Linux Openbox</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/manjaro-linux-openbox-2/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Feb 2014 13:51:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/manjaro-linux-openbox-2/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3806/12793203984_9b37719f63_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Upload from Dropbox February 26, 2014 at 01:46PM http://flic.kr/p/kuuvQu, February 26, 2014 at 01:47PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>